// The ascent of a line in lu with its extra leading folded in: the line is (asc + desc) * pct / 100 tall, the descent stays, and what is left above it is the ascent, never below 0. An unset pct (-1) is quill_layout_line_percent, single spacing.
// By hand with asc 896 and desc 192: 100 percent gives 1088 - 192 = 896; 150 percent gives 1632 - 192 = 1440; 10 percent gives 108 - 192, which is below 0, so 0.
layout_paragraph_leading(int leading_ascent, int leading_descent, int leading_percent) {
  if(leading_percent < 0) {
    leading_percent = (import quill_layout_line_percent);
  }
  int top = fixed_point_maximum((leading_ascent + leading_descent) * leading_percent / 100 - leading_descent, 0);
} return int top;
